Hi Peter and Chris.

Have you tried installing ergm from source?  (ergm is the new  
statnet, basically.  It's brand-new on CRAN.)  Try going to CRAN,  
downloading the source for ergm, gunzipping and untarring it, then  
installing using R CMD INSTALL ergm.  Once back in R, type library 
(ergm) and see if you get the same error.  If any part of that was  
unclear, let me know -- I'm happy to expand on any part of it.

Alternatively, you can try install.packages("statnet") now.  The new  
statnet (also newly on CRAN) is basically just a shell that requires  
several other packages, including ergm and network.  So this is  
probably the easiest road to take.  More on this soon in another email!

I used to have a similar problem on my mac as well, and I made some  
sort of hack to get around it -- I think I set up a symbolic link  
called 'i386' in the /Library/.../libs directory that pointed to  
'ppc', but I don't recall the details and I can't find my old hack at  
the moment.  But in any case, if you're still stuck after the ergm  
stuff, I'm sure we can come up with some workaround! :)

Dave


