From handcock at stat.washington.edu  Mon Jan 21 17:55:22 2008
From: handcock at stat.washington.edu (Mark S. Handcock)
Date: Thu Jun  7 11:20:28 2018
Subject: [statnet_help] simulating graphs from a model with parameters
	given
In-Reply-To: <2869.24.131.194.178.1200966385.squirrel@www.stat.cmu.edu>
Message-ID: <C3BA8D0A.148FB%handcock@stat.washington.edu>

Avranil,

It is. Take a look the example in the help e.g., ?simulate.formula

e.g.,

     g.use <- network(16,density=0.1,directed=FALSE)
     #
     # Starting from this network let's draw 5 realizations
     # of a edges and 2-star network
     #
     g.sim <- simulate(g.use~edges+kstar(2),nsim=5,theta0=c(-1.8,0.03),
                       burnin=100000,interval=1000)
     g.sim

Best,

Mark


