From dhunter at stat.psu.edu  Tue Jan 22 23:52:50 2008
From: dhunter at stat.psu.edu (David Hunter)
Date: Thu Jun  7 11:20:28 2018
Subject: [statnet_help] CRAN packages, users guide drafts
Message-ID: <97046D32-CE61-4CC9-8E21-073CCEC8A23D@stat.psu.edu>

Hi all.  First, I'm sorry the statnet team has been slow to answer  
emails lately.  We've been frantically tying up loose ends to release  
several packages on CRAN and also finish a set of eight manuscripts  
that will be published very soon as a special volume of the online  
Journal of Statistical Software.

To keep things short for now...

Most of the old "statnet" functionality is now in a CRAN package  
called "ergm".  However, "statnet" still exists, as a CRAN package  
that basically just loads several other packages (including ergm).

So the easiest thing to try is to go to R and type install.packages 
("statnet").  This should install all of the required packages.*   
Then type library(statnet) to load them.  If instead you like to  
install from the source code, you can find that on CRAN.

Also, a set of draft manuscripts for the aforementioned JSS volume  
can be found at http://statnetproject.org/users_guide.shtml
Of course, we'll send out another email when the final versions are  
available at the JSS website.

Undoubtedly there will be more info to follow in the near future.   
We'd love to hear any bug reports of course...

Dave Hunter

* recently several of us have had troubles getting the  
install.packages() function to work.  The only thing we all had in  
common was that we were using a version of R older than the latest,  
which is 2.6.1, and after we upgraded the problem went away.   
However, upgrading can sometimes bring its own set of issues (it  
certainly did for me on my mac!), on which perhaps more in a later  
post if others have similar problems!



