This could be done using the snow package without a lot of difficulty. 
I haven't looked into it heretofore because (1) no one had requested it, 
(2) most of the machines I work on are old-fashioned, single processor 
beasts (and hence I don't have a very extensive repertoire of testing 
machines), and (3) the gains from parallel processing are usually pretty 
modest compared to the benefits of improving the underlying algorithms 
(where possible).  If there's demand for it, I'll look into what it 
would take to start integrating this into future versions of sna...in 
principle, it is simple enough, but one must be careful about 
introducing unforeseen maintenance issues (especially if R's support for 
parallel processing is in an unstable state).  I would feel more 
comfortable about putting this in at the package level if the R core 
team had committed to a parallelization paradigm.  (Which they might 
have, though I am unaware of it.)

Thanks for the suggestion,

-Carter

