Dear Jack,

Such embarrassingly parallel replications are easy in principle to do. 
I've tried (and failed) to get any of the R parallelization packages 
working; RPVM just hangs, and our MPI implementation is MPICH rather 
than LAM-MPI (I've never got the latter to work properly). I'd go along 
with Carter's comments, that parallelization is not handled very 
well/stably in R as yet. The ugly hack is to call an R script from the 
command line, using some kind of MPI-enabled shell. I've used (for 
example) MPI-enabled Ruby or Python interpreters (the latter using pypar 
and RPy).

Best
Simon

