has not been developed for directed networks very well. In most cases the
"constraints=~degrees" option is better. Alternatively, we recommend that
you use 'outdegree' or 'indegree' instead.

The bug is a print error as it prints out the warning when it is used with a
directed network. It will be fixed and propagated to CRAN in a few days.

Best,

Mark

